[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "King's Gambit"]
[Variation "King's Gambit: Falkbeer Countergambit"]
[ECO "C31"]
[Character "sharp,tactical"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "counter-gambit,centre-pawns"]
[Kind "gambit"]

1. e4 e5 2. f4 d5 { The Falkbeer: instead of taking White's pawn, Black offers one back and fights for the centre at once. }
3. exd5 e4 { The e-pawn cramps White's knight, which cannot use f3. }
4. d3 Nf6 { Develops with an attack on the pawn on d5 and keeps the e4 pawn defended. }
5. dxe4 Nxe4 { Black has regained the pawn and the knight sits in the centre. }
6. Nf3 Bc5 { Develops with an eye on g1 and f2. White still has to find a safe place for the king. }
7. Qe2 Bf5 { Pins nothing yet but threatens ...Nc3-style forks and develops the last minor piece with tempo. } *
